<title>USA: W.House's Yellen says doesn't 2nd guess FX market.</title>
<headline>W.House's Yellen says doesn't 2nd guess FX market.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House Economic Adviser Janet Yellen said markets dictate the value of the dollar and her job is not to second guess the greenback's trading levels.</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar's value is determined in markets and what our job is is not to try to second guess those markets but to try to make sure the fundamentals for our economy are strong and in place and let markets work,&quot; she said in an interview on CNBC.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
</text>
